// FlatGeobuf - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// FlatGeobuf: the format GDAL 3.4 and QGIS 3.30 moved to, which
// replaced GeoPackage's JSON sidecar with a header inside the
// file. Magic, version, header type, then a bounding box.
//
// There is no greeting in this file, and the reason is worth
// seeing once. The magic is 0A 0D 0D 0A -- so the first eight
// bytes of this dump are two newlines with four bytes between
// them, which is why FlatGeobuf looks like a text file that has
// a very short first line. The rest is a geometry type and
// padding: no name, no description, no comment field. A
// `Hello World!` in any of them would be a file no reader
// accepts, so this one is a correct header with nothing to say.
//
// flatgeobuf: 106 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 0A 0D 0D 0A 03 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0000
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 3F F0 00 00 00 00 00 00 3F F0 |......?.......?.|   <- 0010
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0020
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0030
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0040
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 |................|   <- 0050
// 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00                   |..........|   <- 0060
